Function build_prompt_package:
- assemble shared prompts plus run-specific prompts for four modes, but only inject tool-planning blocks when the prompt is actually planning tools
- inject only useful context blocks: match overview, context bundle, task-specific fields, baseline, calibration, reference summary, session memory, tool facts, and localization mappings
- describe `recommend_full_build` as a fixed-slot array workflow whose filled span can be limited by `recommendation_count`
- harden tool-planning instructions so the model must return exactly one top-level JSON object, use `tool_name`/`arguments`, and avoid leaking final-answer fields during planning
- keep `game_status` prompts compact by stripping duplicated champion profiles from the context block and by transforming the appendix into a prompt-only compact snapshot
- treat enemy-side replan requests as the same `recommend_full_build` workflow shape rather than introducing a separate prompt mode
- surface tool facts in a more ID-centric way, especially for fuzzy catalog search, slug resolution, and category-based item-ID listings
- keep compare-build and tool-derived slug context aligned with the workflow while skipping empty build/rune sections that would waste tokens
